  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has aromatic leaves that can be used to teach about plant scents and essential oils. The leaves are evergreen, making it an excellent subject for lessons on different types of foliage. Its small, yellow-green flowers bloom in clusters and attract various pollinators, providing a practical example for studying plant-pollinator interactions. The tree also produces small, dark fruits that can be used to discuss seed dispersal methods.",
